# Theme Sandbox (Mandatory for UI Work)

**Port 3333 is reserved for the theme sandbox.** No other service may bind it.

## When this applies

Any web page, site, component, theme, color, palette, token, layout, or styling change.

## Agent obligations

1. Load skill `zoo-theme-sandbox` before implementing visual UI.
2. Locate `theme-sandbox/` (or `web/theme-sandbox/`); copy from `Elevated-Applicant/web/theme-sandbox/` if missing.
3. Start sandbox (WSL only): `npm run theme-sandbox` from hub or `Elevated-Applicant/web`, or `node scripts/theme-sandbox.mjs`.
4. Prototype in sandbox HTML first — **never** push unvetted UI directly into framework code.
5. Validate WCAG 2.1 AA + light/dark in sandbox, then port finalized tokens to production.
6. Use browser MCP to verify `http://localhost:3333` when sandbox is running.

